# KeyboardKoala

- Prefer small, pure functions. Keep side effects at the edges (Tauri commands, React event handlers).
- Do not commit secrets, personal paths, private URLs, tokens, or real user configs.
- User config lives only under `~/.config/keyboardkoala`. Examples stay under `examples/config/`.
- Keep Tauri capabilities minimal. Scope filesystem access to the config directory.
- Shell-like actions use `run` as an argv array only (no shell string). Never add `sh -c` helpers.
- Code and commit messages in English. User-facing UI may be German.
- Prefer stable dependency versions already pinned in lockfiles over bleeding-edge releases.
- For commit message format, follow `.cursor/rules/git-commits.mdc`.
- For SemVer and git tags, follow `.cursor/rules/versioning.mdc`.
